@startuml auth
title Authentication and logout with one session token
autonumber
actor "User" as User
participant "hermes (CLI / TUI)" as Client
database "Local credential store" as Local
participant "hermes-document-service" as HDS
participant "hermes-notification-service" as HNS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Sign in ==
User -> Client : hermes auth login
Client --> User : Request credentials using the selected authentication method
User -> Client : Provide credentials securely
Client -> HDS : Authenticate(credentials) over TLS
HDS -> DB : Find active account and verify credentials
alt Invalid credentials or inactive account
  HDS --> Client : Authentication failed; no session token
  Client --> User : Show authentication error
else Valid credentials
  HDS -> HDS : Generate a cryptographically random opaque token
  HDS -> DB : Create session (id, user_id, token_hash,\ncreated_at, expires_at, revoked_at=null)
  DB --> HDS : Session persisted
  HDS --> Client : Session token and expires_at
  Client -> Local : Securely store token, expiry and server identity
  alt Local storage succeeded
    Local --> Client : Saved
    Client --> User : Signed in
  else Local storage failed
    Local --> Client : Storage error
    Client -> HDS : Logout(token); attempt to revoke newly created session
    HDS -> DB : Mark session revoked if request arrives
    Client --> User : Sign-in not saved; report cleanup outcome
  end
end
note over Client, DB
  Exactly one token: no access/refresh token pair.
  The server stores only its hash; the raw token is a bearer credential.
  Never log the token or credentials; do not pass secrets as CLI arguments.
  Credential method and session lifetime are to be specified.
end note

== Execute a short command or open TUI ==
User -> Client : Run a protected command or open hermes
Client -> Local : Read session for the selected server
alt No local token
  Local --> Client : Not signed in
  Client --> User : Ask user to run hermes auth login
else Token available
  Local --> Client : Token and expiry
  Client -> HDS : Protected request with session token over TLS
  HDS -> DB : Find session by token hash; check expiry,\nrevocation and active user
  alt Session valid
    HDS -> DB : Check operation permissions and execute request
    HDS --> Client : Result or permission denied
    Client --> User : Display result
  else Session expired, revoked or unknown
    HDS --> Client : Unauthenticated
    Client -> Local : Remove rejected token if it is still the stored token
    Client --> User : Sign in again; no automatic token refresh
  end
end
note over Client, HDS
  Ending a command or closing TUI does not revoke the session.
  Permission denied does not invalidate an authenticated session.
  A network error does not remove a stored token.
end note

== Authenticate requests to notification service ==
Client -> HNS : Inbox request with the same token over TLS
HNS -> HDS : ValidateSession(token) over authenticated internal TLS
HDS -> DB : Check token hash, expiry, revocation and active user
alt Session valid
  HDS --> HNS : Authenticated user_id and session expiry
  HNS -> HNS : Apply recipient and current access checks
  HNS --> Client : Inbox result or permission denied
else Session invalid
  HDS --> HNS : Unauthenticated
  HNS --> Client : Unauthenticated; sign-in required
else Validation service unavailable
  HNS --> Client : Temporarily unavailable; no access granted
end
note over HDS, HNS
  Proposed integration: notification service delegates session validation
  to document service on each request; no positive validation cache initially.
  Both services use the same session; notification service issues no token.
  Workspace permissions are checked separately from authentication.
end note

== Sign out of the current session ==
User -> Client : hermes auth logout / Sign out in TUI
Client -> Local : Read current token
alt No local token
  Client --> User : Already signed out locally
else Token available
  Local --> Client : Current token
  Client -> HDS : Logout(token) over TLS
  alt Server reachable
    HDS -> DB : Revoke session identified by token hash, if present
    HDS --> Client : Signed out (also for expired, revoked or unknown token)
    Client -> Local : Remove this token without deleting a newer login
    Client --> User : Signed out after local removal succeeds
  else Server unreachable or outcome unknown
    Client -> Local : Remove this token without deleting a newer login
    Client --> User : Signed out locally; server revocation not confirmed
    note over Client, DB
      A server session that was not revoked remains valid until expiry.
      Local deletion alone does not revoke copies of the token.
    end note
  end
end
note over Client, Local
  If local deletion fails, report the failure rather than claiming success.
  Cancel authenticated TUI polling and return to the signed-out screen.
  Logout affects only this session, not sessions on other devices.
  Requests already authorized before revocation may finish.
end note
@enduml
